{"nodes": [{"id": "readme_type_react_monorepo", "label": "type-react prep monorepo", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_twinned_demos", "label": "Four twinned demos (React vs Angular)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The same four components are built twice on one framework-agnostic core so the only remaining difference is the reactivity model \u2014 that isolates exactly what interviewers probe when they ask whether a React developer can do Angular or vice versa."}, {"id": "readme_packages_core", "label": "packages/core (framework-agnostic logic)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Kept framework-agnostic and consumed from dist/ so both labs share one implementation and the 18 unit tests double as the live-coding drill specs."}, {"id": "readme_apps_react_lab", "label": "apps/react-lab (React 19 + Vite + Vitest)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_apps_angular_lab", "label": "apps/angular-lab (Angular 20, standalone, zoneless)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Deliberately ships no zone.js at all, using provideZonelessChangeDetection(), because signals-plus-zoneless is the highest-leverage Angular differentiator few candidates can speak to credibly."}, {"id": "readme_apps_next_lab", "label": "apps/next-lab (Next.js 15 App Router)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_apps_nest_api", "label": "apps/nest-api (NestJS 11)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_demo_typeahead", "label": "Typeahead demo", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Chosen because it forces race conditions, cancellation and cleanup into the open: React solves it with useDebouncedValue + AbortController, Angular with debounceTime + switchMap and again with resource()."}, {"id": "readme_demo_product_table", "label": "Product table demo", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "useReducer + useMemo versus signal + computed \u2014 picked to expose derived state, memoisation and coupled state invariants such as filter changes resetting the page."}, {"id": "readme_demo_virtual_list", "label": "Virtual list demo", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Same scroll/slice/spacer maths in both frameworks, so the only difference visible is how the derived slice is recomputed; the point is rendering 50k rows without jank."}, {"id": "readme_demo_store_undo_redo", "label": "Store + undo/redo demo", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "useSyncExternalStore versus subscribe-to-signal, to demonstrate what state libraries actually are underneath."}], "edges": [{"source": "readme_type_react_monorepo", "target": "readme_twinned_demos", "relat